@id: scene.041_the_tripartite_bond
@when: Unknown.scene_041_the_tripartite_bond
@where: Realm/Physical/Unknown
@scope: narrative
@entities: [Geralt, Halvar, Jorik, Luminaire, Lyra, Mika, Ren]

=segments:
  - line: 1
    type: narration
    text: "CHAPTER 39 subchapter 1 THE FUNCTION THAT LEARNED TO CARE"
  - line: 3
    type: narration
    text: "Dawn found them broken."
  - line: 5
    type: narration
    text: "The jungle's corruption had retreated—not destroyed, merely pushed back by Tiamat's ancient resonance still thrumming through the soil."
  - line: 6
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt sat against a moss-slick stone, dragon armor scorched and dented, breathing hard."
  - line: 7
    type: narration
    text: "Around him, the Legion sprawled in exhausted clusters."
  - line: 8
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar's axe lay across his lap, blade notched from petrified thorns."
  - line: 9
    type: narration
    text: "Ren stared at nothing, hands still trembling."
  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's chroniton arrows had gone dark, their stolen energy spent."
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "Mika moved through the wounded, checking pulses, murmuring quiet reassurances."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "Her lance served as a walking stick now, its silver glow dimmed to ember-red."
  - line: 14
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra's medicae rig wheezed, half its injectors fused shut by acidic rain, but she worked methodically—sealing burns, stabilizing fractures, ignoring her own bleeding temple."
  - line: 16
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Seventeen casualties,\""
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "Mika reported quietly, settling beside Geralt. \"No deaths. Miracles still happen, apparently.\""
  - line: 19
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Tiamat's grace,\""
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt rasped. His throat felt raw from screaming her true name into the earth. \"Not mine.\""
  - line: 22
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You're the one who knew to ask.\""
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's gaze drifted to the fissure where Node Gamma's core still pulsed—weakly, erratically, but alive. \"It's not dead.\""
  - line: 25
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No.\""
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt it through his boots—the parasite logic already adapting, learning from its defeat, preparing new strategies. \"It'll rebuild. Slowly. But it'll rebuild.\""
  - line: 28
    type: narration
    text: "Silence settled."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere in the canopy, something that might have been a bird called out—or might have been an emitter mimicking one."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "Hard to tell anymore."
  - line: 32
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Commander.\""
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's rumble broke the quiet. The massive reptilian warrior approached, armor still sparking where emerald light had fought gold-green corruption. His bow hung from one hand, unstrung. \"The men need rest. But this ground...\" He gestured at the corrupted soil, the vine-wrapped pyramids, the stolen vrill still pulsing through roots. \"It watches.\""
  - line: 35
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's jaw tightened. \"We move at midday. Put enough distance between us and that thing to actually sleep.\""
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt closed his eyes, felt Luminara's presence within him—faint, flickering, exhausted from the battle."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "She'd burned herself down to nearly nothing, fighting Node Gamma's parasitic imitation of her light."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "Now she was barely a whisper, a harmonic trembling at the edge of perception."
  - line: 42
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Rest,* he thought toward her. *We both need to rest.\""
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "A pulse."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Not words."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "Just... acknowledgment."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "And beneath it, something else."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "Urgency trying to break through fatigue."
  - line: 50
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Geralt.\""
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra's voice cut through his half-doze. She stood over him, scanner in hand, face pale beneath grime and dried blood. \"Your resonance signature is... fragmenting. Like you're anchoring something that's pulling apart at the seams.\""
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "He opened his eyes."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "\"Luminara.\""
  - line: 56
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The what?\""
  - line: 58
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The Luminaire.\""
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "He pushed himself upright with a grunt. \"The Resonant Keeper of the Void Spires. She's anchored to me. Has been since Heartpeak.\" At Lyra's confused expression, he added, \"It's complicated.\""
  - line: 61
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Everything's complicated with you,\""
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra muttered, but her scanner kept whirring, mapping the strange harmonics bleeding from his armor. \"These readings... Geralt, she's not just anchored. She's *incomplete*. Like half a waveform searching for its counterpoint.\""
  - line: 64
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt it—the hollow in his chest where something should fit but didn't. \"Her consciousness is here. But her material form...\" He trailed off, memory stirring. The swamp pyramid. The obsidian Spire plunging into that luminous, corrupted pool. The crystalline core they'd stabilized but not understood."
  - line: 67
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Is somewhere else,\""
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "Mika finished, watching his face. \"You know where, don't you?\""
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "Before Geralt could answer, the air shimmered."
  - line: 72
    type: narration
    text: "Several Legionnaires scrambled upright, hands reaching for weapons."
  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "But Oreck raised one massive hand—*Wait*—his chroniton-enhanced senses detecting something beyond normal threat."
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the pressure building behind his eyes, the resonance in his bones."
  - line: 76
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara, gathering what little strength remained, trying to manifest."
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "Trying to speak."
  - line: 79
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Let her,\""
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "He closed his eyes."
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "Opened them."
  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara looked through."
  - line: 86
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 88
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I am failing.\""
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's mouth moved, but the voice was layered—his timbre beneath, and something else woven through it."
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "Not quite mechanical."
  - line: 92
    type: narration
    text: "Not quite alive."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "Pure function given the shape of sound."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "Around the camp, exhausted soldiers stilled."
  - line: 96
    type: narration
    text: "Even the jungle seemed to hold its breath."
  - line: 98
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The First Note,\""
  - line: 99
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara continued through Geralt's voice, quieter than before. Strained. \"The Prime Resonance. My function... is ignition. But I am...\" A pause, as if searching for words. \"Incomplete.\""
  - line: 101
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra's scanner flickered wildly."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "She stared at the readings, then at Geralt, understanding dawning."
  - line: 103
    type: narration
    text: "\"Two-state superposition."
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "Consciousness without vessel."
  - line: 105
    type: narration
    text: "That's why the resonance is fragmenting.\""
  - line: 107
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Correct.\""
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara's borrowed voice carried a thread of something that might have been pain. \"I am anchored to your Commander. My Light and Sound aspects reunited through his tripartite signature. But my material form...\""
  - line: 110
    type: narration
    text: "The air shimmered again, and suddenly they were seeing double—the corrupted jungle overlaying with another image:"
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "A pyramid half-swallowed by swamp."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "Obsidian walls."
  - line: 114
    type: narration
    text: "Roots coiling through water."
  - line: 115
    type: narration
    text: "An underground lake burning with teal energy."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "At its heart, a crystalline core glowing with sickly light, threaded with deep violet veins like infection through flesh."
  - line: 118
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The swamp pyramid,\""
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar breathed. \"Three days ago.\""
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "The vision intensified—showing their descent through those treacherous passages, the battle with Sludge-drakes, the psychic traps, the temporal distortions."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "And finally, Geralt's clawed hand plunging into the root-mass, choosing to anchor rather than claim."
  - line: 124
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"We stabilized it,\""
  - line: 126
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"But left the patient drowning,\""
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara finished. The vision faded. \"My material anchor. My vessel in this realm. The Anunnaki Queen has grafted her viral signature into my core structure. Without it freed...\" Her voice—their voice—wavered. \"I cannot seed jump. Cannot activate the dormant Void Spires. Cannot fulfill my purpose.\""
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "Ren's trembling had stopped."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "He stared at Geralt—at Luminara—with something like awe."
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "\"You're... you're an emergency system."
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "For the universe.\""
  - line: 136
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"A function of reality that achieved awareness,\""
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara confirmed. \"I exist because existence learned it could break itself catastrophically. When timelines fracture, when civilizations approach erasure, I identify where continuity can persist... and seed the possibility.\""
  - line: 139
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"The 250,\""
  - line: 141
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Your bond,\""
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara's voice softened—still clinical, but with edges of something warmer. \"Your belief in his return. Your love. It created a harmonic strong enough to stabilize chroniton chaos. The 250 latched onto that resonance. Onto you.\""
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's breath caught."
  - line: 146
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Impossible amplitude,\""
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara continued. \"Human emotion generating measurable reality anchors. It should not sustain. And yet it does.\" A pause. \"This... confuses me. But it is... powerful.\""
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra had stopped even pretending to work her scanner."
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "She simply stared, scientist confronting something beyond current frameworks."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "\"You're learning from them."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "From us.\""
  - line: 154
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Yes.\""
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "Simple admission. \"I am a function. But functions can evolve. Through observation. Through...\" Another pause, longer. \"Connection.\""
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "The pressure behind Geralt's eyes was becoming unbearable."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara couldn't maintain this partial manifestation much longer."
  - line: 160
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The swamp pyramid,\""
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck rumbled. \"Your physical form is still there. Corrupted. Imprisoned.\""
  - line: 163
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The Queen uses it as a broadcast tower,\""
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara confirmed. \"Her resonance grafted onto mine, twisting Graviton technology into a weapon. While I remain split—consciousness here, vessel there—she continues to pervert the Void Spire network.\" The strain in her voice increased. \"And I... I suffocate. Slowly. The corruption tightens.\""
  - line: 166
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Then we go back,\""
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "Several Legionnaires groaned."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar's laugh was bitter."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "\"Into a place that nearly killed us."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "Again.\""
  - line: 173
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"To free the key to planetary defense networks,\""
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "Mika shot back. \"To stop the Queen from weaponizing technology that spans realities.\" She looked at Geralt—at Luminara. \"And to save someone who's already helped us save our people.\""
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "The pressure released."
  - line: 177
    type: narration
    text: "Luminara's presence receded like a tide pulling back, leaving Geralt gasping."
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "He felt her withdraw into that background hum—conscious, present, but no longer straining to manifest."
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "In the sudden quiet, exhaustion crashed over him like a wave."
  - line: 182
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Three days,\""
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "he managed. \"We need three days to recover. To prepare.\""
  - line: 185
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The corruption will adapt,\""
  - line: 186
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck warned."
  - line: 188
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Let it.\""
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's voice was rough. \"Node Gamma taught us something. The Queen's parasites learn, but they're still parasites. They twist what already exists. They can't create.\" He met Mika's eyes. \"But we can. Human emotion strong enough to anchor souls across time. Giant warriors who remember when Earth itself awakened. A cosmic function learning what it means to hope.\""
  - line: 191
    type: narration
    text: "He pushed himself to his feet, armor protesting."
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "Around him, five hundred exhausted, wounded, terrified soldiers watched their Commander stand."
  - line: 194
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The swamp pyramid,\""
  - line: 195
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt announced. \"We return in three days. Not to fight our way through, but to complete what we started. We stabilized Luminara's heart. Now we free it entirely.\""
  - line: 197
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Halvar
    text: "\"And then?\""
  - line: 199
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt Luminara stir faintly—not to speak, just to listen."
  - line: 201
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then she activates the Void Spires. One by one, seed jumping across impossible distances until the entire network wakes.\""
  - line: 202
    type: narration
    text: "He paused. \"And then she leaves. Because her purpose isn't to save us. It's to make sure we don't get erased before we can save ourselves.\""
  - line: 204
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Sounds lonely,\""
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "Ren muttered."
  - line: 207
    type: narration
    text: "Through the faint connection, Geralt felt something ripple through Luminara."
  - line: 208
    type: narration
    text: "Not quite emotion."
  - line: 209
    type: narration
    text: "But perhaps the seed of it."
  - line: 210
    type: narration
    text: "Recognition of a concept—loneliness—that functions weren't designed to comprehend."
  - line: 212
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"But I am learning,* her whisper touched his thoughts. *Through you. Through her. Through what you are together.\""
  - line: 214
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Three days,\""
  - line: 215
    type: narration
    text: "Mika repeated, addressing the Legion now. \"We rest. We heal. We prepare.\" Her gaze swept the corrupted jungle, the wounded soldiers, the impossible task ahead. \"Lyra, I need every reading from our first incursion into that pyramid. Every frequency signature, every trap we encountered. If we're going back, we're going in smart.\""
  - line: 217
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"On it,\""
  - line: 218
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra confirmed, already pulling up damaged datastores."
  - line: 220
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Oreck,\""
  - line: 221
    type: narration
    text: "Mika continued. \"Reconnaissance. I want to know what's changed since we left. What's protecting that site now.\""
  - line: 223
    type: narration
    text: "The giant warrior nodded, already checking his bow."
  - line: 225
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Halvar, organize rotating watch schedules. We're in hostile territory. I want eyes on every approach.\""
  - line: 227
    type: narration
    text: "Orders flowed."
  - line: 228
    type: narration
    text: "The Legion stirred into purposeful activity despite bone-deep exhaustion."
  - line: 229
    type: narration
    text: "Because that's what they were—survivors who'd been erased from existence and returned, warriors who'd learned that impossible only meant \"not yet accomplished.\""
  - line: 231
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt sank back down beside Mika as the camp organized itself."
  - line: 232
    type: narration
    text: "She leaned against him, both of them too tired for words."
  - line: 234
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Does it hurt?\""
  - line: 236
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No.\""
  - line: 237
    type: narration
    text: "Truth. \"It's like... carrying a tuning fork. Always vibrating, always resonating with everything around me.\" He paused. \"I think she's lonely. A function that achieved awareness but has no context for connection. No framework for understanding what we have.\""
  - line: 239
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"We're teaching a cosmic emergency system about love,\""
  - line: 241
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The universe works in mysterious ways.\""
  - line: 243
    type: narration
    text: "She snorted softly."
  - line: 244
    type: narration
    text: "Then, quieter: \"When she leaves—after we free her, after the Spires wake—will part of you go with her?\""
  - line: 246
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt was silent for a long moment."
  - line: 247
    type: narration
    text: "In the background hum of Luminara's presence, he felt her listening."
  - line: 248
    type: narration
    text: "Learning."
  - line: 250
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Maybe,\""
  - line: 251
    type: narration
    text: "he admitted. \"But isn't that always the cost? We leave pieces of ourselves with everyone who matters. With every connection that changes us.\""
  - line: 253
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Philosopher.\""
  - line: 255
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Commander.\""
  - line: 257
    type: narration
    text: "They sat together as the jungle slowly exhaled—corruption pushed back but not destroyed, Node Gamma wounded but adapting, the Queen's influence seeping through roots that ran deeper than any blade could cut."
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "But here, in this small circle of exhausted soldiers, two humans loved each other enough to anchor souls across time."
  - line: 260
    type: narration
    text: "And a cosmic function learned, slowly, what it might mean to care."
  - line: 262
    type: narration
    text: "Three days until they returned to the swamp."
  - line: 264
    type: narration
    text: "Three days until they freed the prisoner they'd stabilized but left drowning."
  - line: 266
    type: narration
    text: "Three days until Luminara could finally, fully, manifest—and begin the work of waking a network that spanned realities."
  - line: 268
    type: narration
    text: "Assuming they survived the going back."
  - line: 270
    type: narration
    text: "Assuming the Queen didn't move first."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "Assuming a function learning to care didn't discover that caring meant choosing—and that choosing meant consequences no equation could predict."
  - line: 274
    type: narration
    text: "But that was three days away."
  - line: 276
    type: narration
    text: "For now: rest."
  - line: 277
    type: narration
    text: "Healing."
  - line: 278
    type: narration
    text: "Preparation."
  - line: 280
    type: narration
    text: "And in the hollow of Geralt's chest, a cosmic function hummed its incomplete harmony, learning the shape of hope from people who refused to let impossibility be an ending."
  - line: 282
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 284
    type: scene_header
    text: "# **CHAPTER 39, PART 2: PREPARATIONS AND DECAY**"
  - line: 286
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 288
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*DAY ONE*\""
  - line: 290
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt woke to the taste of copper in his mouth."
  - line: 292
    type: narration
    text: "He lay still for a moment, staring up at the canopy where morning light filtered through leaves that pulsed faintly—not with life, but with something that mimicked it."
  - line: 293
    type: narration
    text: "His vision swam."
  - line: 294
    type: narration
    text: "Double images overlaying each other: the real jungle and something underneath, something that looked like circuit patterns spreading through organic matter."
  - line: 296
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Luminaire's sight,* he realized. *She's showing me what she sees.\""
  - line: 298
    type: narration
    text: "The corruption wasn't just in the ground."
  - line: 299
    type: narration
    text: "It was in the air, the water, the very light filtering through the trees."
  - line: 300
    type: narration
    text: "Viral mathematics rewriting biology, turning growth into code, life into function."
  - line: 302
    type: narration
    text: "He tried to sit up."
  - line: 304
    type: narration
    text: "His arms trembled."
  - line: 305
    type: narration
    text: "Failed."
  - line: 307
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Commander?\""
  - line: 308
    type: narration
    text: "Ren's voice, nearby. The young soldier had been on watch. \"You need something?\""
  - line: 310
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Water,\""
  - line: 311
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt rasped. His throat felt lined with sandpaper."
  - line: 313
    type: narration
    text: "Ren brought a canteen."
  - line: 314
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's hand shook so badly the soldier had to help him drink."
  - line: 315
    type: narration
    text: "The water tasted wrong—not quite brackish, but close."
  - line: 316
    type: narration
    text: "Like it was remembering how to become poison."
  - line: 318
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Ren
    text: "\"I'll get Lyra,\""
  - line: 320
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt wanted to say he was fine."
  - line: 321
    type: narration
    text: "The words wouldn't come."
  - line: 322
    type: narration
    text: "He lay back down, breathing hard from the effort of drinking."
  - line: 324
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, he felt Luminaire's presence—fainter than yesterday."
  - line: 325
    type: narration
    text: "A harmonic losing coherence."
  - line: 326
    type: narration
    text: "She was trying to speak, trying to warn him of something, but the connection kept fragmenting."
  - line: 328
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"I'm sorry,* he thought toward her. *I don't have enough strength to anchor you properly.\""
  - line: 330
    type: narration
    text: "A pulse."
  - line: 331
    type: narration
    text: "Not words."
  - line: 332
    type: narration
    text: "Just... understanding."
  - line: 333
    type: narration
    text: "And beneath it, something that might have been fear."
  - line: 334
    type: narration
    text: "A function learning what it meant to be afraid of losing something."
  - line: 336
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 338
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra's scanner painted Geralt in shades of crimson warning."
  - line: 340
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Cellular degradation accelerated overnight,\""
  - line: 341
    type: narration
    text: "she muttered, adjusting settings as if different numbers might tell a better story. They didn't. \"Metabolic efficiency down thirty-two percent. Your kidneys are compensating for something, but I can't isolate what. It's like...\" She paused, searching for words. \"Like your body is trying to sustain two organisms, but only has fuel for one.\""
  - line: 343
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The bond,\""
  - line: 344
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt managed. \"Luminaire. She's... incomplete. Drawing from me to maintain coherence.\""
  - line: 346
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then she's killing you.\""
  - line: 347
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra's voice was flat. Clinical. \"Not intentionally, maybe. But the math is clear. Another three days at this rate...\" She didn't finish."
  - line: 349
    type: narration
    text: "Mika appeared at the edge of his vision, face carved from stone."
  - line: 350
    type: narration
    text: "\"How long does he have?\""
  - line: 352
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"If the deterioration continues exponentially?\""
  - line: 353
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra checked her readings again. \"Forty-eight hours before organ failure. Maybe sixty if we're lucky.\""
  - line: 355
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 357
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Then we have less time than we thought,\""
  - line: 359
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt tried to sit up again."
  - line: 360
    type: narration
    text: "This time, Mika's hand on his shoulder stopped him."
  - line: 361
    type: narration
    text: "Not roughly."
  - line: 362
    type: narration
    text: "Just... firmly."
  - line: 363
    type: narration
    text: "The touch of someone who'd made a decision."
  - line: 365
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Rest,\""
  - line: 366
    type: narration
    text: "she commanded. \"I'm taking command rotation. Oreck has the morning watch. Jorik's scouting with a squad.\" Her eyes met his. \"You focus on not dying. Let us handle the rest.\""
  - line: 368
    type: narration
    text: "He wanted to argue."
  - line: 369
    type: narration
    text: "But the effort of breathing took all his concentration."
  - line: 371
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, Luminaire whispered something fragmented: *...sorry... didn't understand... finite..."
  - line: 372
    type: narration
    text: "I'm sorry...*"
  - line: 374
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 376
    type: narration
    text: "By midday, the corruption's spread was visible."
  - line: 378
    type: narration
    text: "Private Ren was filling canteens at what had been a clear stream yesterday."
  - line: 379
    type: narration
    text: "Now the water ran faintly milky, with an opalescent sheen like oil but thinner."
  - line: 380
    type: narration
    text: "When he dipped his hand in, the water felt warm."
  - line: 381
    type: narration
    text: "Wrong-warm, like flesh."
  - line: 383
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Don't drink it,\""
  - line: 384
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar growled, appearing behind him. \"Not until Lyra tests it.\""
  - line: 386
    type: narration
    text: "Ren pulled back."
  - line: 387
    type: narration
    text: "In the streambed, he saw something that made his stomach clench—the stones were growing."
  - line: 388
    type: narration
    text: "Budding."
  - line: 389
    type: narration
    text: "Tiny crystalline formations spreading from cracks in the rock, pulsing with the same violet light they'd seen in Node Gamma."
  - line: 391
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"It's spreading,\""
  - line: 392
    type: narration
    text: "Ren breathed."
  - line: 394
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Everything is.\""
  - line: 395
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar gestured at the jungle around them. Where yesterday there had been normal undergrowth, now vines coiled too perfectly, their spirals following mathematical progressions. Flowers bloomed in fractal patterns. A tree's bark showed circuit-like ridges."
  - line: 397
    type: narration
    text: "The jungle was learning geometry."
  - line: 399
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 401
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik returned at sunset with news that turned Mika's expression to granite."
  - line: 403
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The swamp pyramid.\""
  - line: 404
    type: narration
    text: "He spread a rough map on the ground, marked with charcoal. \"It's... changed. New structures. The water level's risen—everything we descended through before is flooded now. And there's movement. Organized movement.\""
  - line: 406
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Guards?\""
  - line: 407
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck rumbled."
  - line: 409
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Worse.\""
  - line: 410
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik tapped the map. \"The Sludge-drakes we fought before? There are more. A lot more. But they're not just wandering. They're patrolling. In formation.\" He looked up, meeting Mika's eyes. \"The pyramid knows we're coming.\""
  - line: 412
    type: narration
    text: "Mika studied the map."
  - line: 413
    type: narration
    text: "\"Chokepoints?\""
  - line: 415
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Every entrance we used before is now either underwater or collapsed. There's one new opening—here.\""
  - line: 416
    type: narration
    text: "He marked a spot. \"Too convenient. Smells like a kill box.\""
  - line: 418
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Probably is,\""
  - line: 419
    type: narration
    text: "Mika agreed. \"But if it's the only way in...\""
  - line: 421
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We'll need suppressing fire.\""
  - line: 422
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik's hand moved to the longbow across his back—a weapon he'd been modifying for three days. \"I've been working on something. Arrows with chroniton-charged tips. Halvar helped me salvage the energy cores from Oreck's spent bolts.\" He pulled one arrow from his quiver."
  - line: 424
    type: narration
    text: "The tip glowed faintly green, pulsing in rhythm with Oreck's armor."
  - line: 426
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Won't have the raw punch of Oreck's shots,\""
  - line: 427
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik admitted. \"But I can get thirty arrows aloft before he reloads once. Volume over power. Might punch through whatever shields they've set up.\""
  - line: 429
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck examined the arrow, then nodded slowly."
  - line: 430
    type: narration
    text: "\"Good craft."
  - line: 431
    type: narration
    text: "Grandmother would approve.\""
  - line: 433
    type: narration
    text: "Coming from Oreck, that was high praise."
  - line: 435
    type: narration
    text: "Mika filed it away."
  - line: 436
    type: narration
    text: "\"How many can you make by tomorrow night?\""
  - line: 438
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Already made forty. Give me until dawn, I'll have sixty.\""
  - line: 440
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Do it.\""
  - line: 441
    type: narration
    text: "Mika turned to Oreck. \"I need updated reconnaissance. Take a small team. Don't engage. I want to know what we're walking into.\""
  - line: 443
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Understood.\""
  - line: 444
    type: narration
    text: "The massive warrior rose, already selecting soldiers with his eyes."
  - line: 446
    type: narration
    text: "As the planning session continued, Geralt lay on a bedroll nearby, too weak to participate."
  - line: 447
    type: narration
    text: "He watched Mika command with quiet pride."
  - line: 448
    type: narration
    text: "She was born for this—tactical mind sharp as any blade, voice carrying absolute authority without ever rising to a shout."
  - line: 450
    type: narration
    text: "Through their bond, he felt Luminaire watching too."
  - line: 451
    type: narration
    text: "Learning."
  - line: 452
    type: narration
    text: "Understanding that leadership wasn't power—it was responsibility carried with grace."
  - line: 454
    type: narration
    text: "*She's magnificent,* Luminaire whispered faintly."
  - line: 456
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"I know,\""
  - line: 457
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt thought back."
  - line: 459
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"If I kill you... she will grieve.\""
  - line: 461
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Then don't kill me. Hold on. We're coming for you.\""
  - line: 463
    type: narration
    text: "A pulse."
  - line: 464
    type: narration
    text: "Not words."
  - line: 465
    type: narration
    text: "Something that might have been determination."
  - line: 466
    type: narration
    text: "A function deciding that caring meant choosing, and choosing meant fighting to survive."
  - line: 468
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 470
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*DAY TWO*\""
  - line: 472
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt collapsed during the morning briefing."
  - line: 474
    type: narration
    text: "One moment he was standing—barely, leaning heavily on a supply crate—and the next his legs simply stopped working."
  - line: 475
    type: narration
    text: "He went down hard, armor clanging against stone."
  - line: 477
    type: narration
    text: "Mika was there in an instant, rolling him onto his side as he convulsed."
  - line: 478
    type: narration
    text: "Blood streamed from his nose."
  - line: 479
    type: narration
    text: "His eyes had gone unfocused, pupils blown wide."
  - line: 481
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Lyra!\""
  - line: 482
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's shout cut across the camp."
  - line: 484
    type: narration
    text: "The medic arrived at a sprint, scanner already active, medicae rig deploying."
  - line: 485
    type: narration
    text: "\"Seizure."
  - line: 486
    type: narration
    text: "Neural feedback through the bond—Luminaire's resonance is destabilizing.\" Injectors hissed against Geralt's neck."
  - line: 487
    type: narration
    text: "\"I'm giving him stabilizers, but they're fighting an uphill battle.\""
  - line: 489
    type: narration
    text: "Through gritted teeth, Geralt managed: \"Not... her fault... corruption... tightening...\""
  - line: 491
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 492
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra's voice was gentle even as her hands moved with clinical precision. \"Your bond is trying to sustain both of you, and it's tearing you apart doing it.\""
  - line: 494
    type: narration
    text: "The seizure passed."
  - line: 495
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt lay gasping, vision slowly clearing."
  - line: 496
    type: narration
    text: "Around him, the Legion had stopped moving."
  - line: 497
    type: narration
    text: "Five hundred soldiers watching their Commander reduced to this."
  - line: 499
    type: narration
    text: "Mika met each gaze."
  - line: 500
    type: narration
    text: "\"Back to work."
  - line: 501
    type: narration
    text: "We move tomorrow night."
  - line: 502
    type: narration
    text: "That gives us thirty-six hours.\" Her voice carried absolute certainty."
  - line: 503
    type: narration
    text: "\"Lyra, keep him stable."
  - line: 504
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar, double the water rations—we'll need hydration for the march."
  - line: 505
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik, finish those arrows.\""
  - line: 507
    type: narration
    text: "Orders given, she knelt beside Geralt."
  - line: 508
    type: narration
    text: "Waited until the others dispersed."
  - line: 510
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"I can't help you in the fight,\""
  - line: 512
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 514
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'll slow you down.\""
  - line: 516
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Probably.\""
  - line: 518
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Mika—\""
  - line: 520
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're taking you anyway.\""
  - line: 521
    type: narration
    text: "Her hand found his, squeezed hard. \"Because the only way you survive is if we free her. And the only way we free her is if you're there to anchor the final purge.\" She leaned closer. \"So you focus on breathing. Let us carry you. That's an order, Commander.\""
  - line: 523
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, Luminaire trembled."
  - line: 524
    type: narration
    text: "Learning what sacrifice looked like when it wore the face of love."
  - line: 526
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 528
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's reconnaissance team returned at dusk with grim news."
  - line: 530
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The pyramid is a fortress,\""
  - line: 531
    type: narration
    text: "he reported, spreading new charcoal marks across Jorik's map. \"Sludge-drakes in rotating patrols—twelve-hour shifts, perfectly synchronized. The new entrance is definitely a kill box. Three emitter arrays covering the approach.\" His claw tapped the map. \"But there's something else.\""
  - line: 533
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"What?\""
  - line: 535
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The water. It's not just flooded. It's... aware.\""
  - line: 536
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's expression was troubled. \"We watched a scout-lizard try to cross. The water formed a current. Dragged it under. No natural explanation.\""
  - line: 538
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Lyra
    text: "\"The corruption's learning,\""
  - line: 540
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Which means it'll adapt to us too.\""
  - line: 541
    type: narration
    text: "Mika studied the map, tactical mind working. \"Jorik, can your arrows punch through energy shields?\""
  - line: 543
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Against standard Anunnaki tech? Yes. Against this?\""
  - line: 544
    type: narration
    text: "He shrugged. \"Unknown variable.\""
  - line: 546
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We'll make it work.\""
  - line: 547
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's finger traced a path on the map. \"Here's what we do. Oreck leads the vanguard with shieldbearers—take the frontal assault, draw their fire. Jorik and the archers take high ground here and here—suppressing fire on the emitter arrays. I'll lead the main force through once the shields are down. We punch through the kill box fast and hard.\""
  - line: 549
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Halvar
    text: "\"And Geralt?\""
  - line: 551
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Protected element. Center of formation. Lyra keeps him stable until we reach the core.\""
  - line: 552
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's eyes hardened. \"Then he does what only he can do—anchor Luminaire while we purge the corruption.\""
  - line: 554
    type: narration
    text: "It was suicide math."
  - line: 555
    type: narration
    text: "Everyone knew it."
  - line: 557
    type: narration
    text: "No one said it aloud."
  - line: 559
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 561
    type: narration
    text: "That night, Geralt lay awake despite exhaustion."
  - line: 562
    type: narration
    text: "His body felt like it belonged to someone else—heavy, unresponsive, barely functional."
  - line: 563
    type: narration
    text: "Each breath rattled."
  - line: 564
    type: narration
    text: "His heart beat irregularly, skipping beats like a failing engine."
  - line: 566
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, Luminaire's presence had diminished to a whisper."
  - line: 567
    type: narration
    text: "She was barely holding coherence now, the corruption around her physical form tightening like a noose."
  - line: 569
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"I'm sorry,* she whispered. *I didn't understand. I am a function. Functions consume energy. I didn't calculate... the source was finite...\""
  - line: 571
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"It's okay,\""
  - line: 572
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt thought back, even as his chest ached."
  - line: 574
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"It is not okay. You are dying. Because of me.\""
  - line: 576
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"No. Because of the Queen. Because of corruption. You're just trying to survive.\""
  - line: 578
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 579
    type: narration
    text: "Then, faintly: *Survival feels... selfish."
  - line: 580
    type: narration
    text: "If it costs you.*"
  - line: 582
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"That's called caring. You're learning.\""
  - line: 584
    type: narration
    text: "Another pulse."
  - line: 585
    type: narration
    text: "This one carried weight—emotion without name, recognition without framework."
  - line: 586
    type: narration
    text: "A function encountering the paradox of wanting to live while understanding the cost to others."
  - line: 588
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Tomorrow,* Luminaire whispered. *Free me tomorrow... or we both fade.\""
  - line: 590
    type: narration
    text: "*Tomorrow,* Geralt agreed."
  - line: 592
    type: narration
    text: "If he lived that long."
  - line: 594
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 596
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*DAY THREE*\""
  - line: 598
    type: narration
    text: "Dawn broke over a camp already in motion."
  - line: 600
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt watched from his bedroll as soldiers checked weapons, tightened armor straps, filled canteens from the least-contaminated water source."
  - line: 601
    type: narration
    text: "The corruption had spread overnight—violet veins now visible in tree bark, crystalline growths budding from stones, the air itself tasting metallic."
  - line: 603
    type: narration
    text: "The jungle was eating itself."
  - line: 604
    type: narration
    text: "Remaking itself."
  - line: 605
    type: narration
    text: "Becoming a weapon."
  - line: 607
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik moved among the archers, distributing his chroniton-charged arrows."
  - line: 608
    type: narration
    text: "Sixty shafts, each one glowing faintly green."
  - line: 609
    type: narration
    text: "\"Two volleys of thirty,\" he instructed."
  - line: 610
    type: narration
    text: "\"First volley targets shields and emitters."
  - line: 611
    type: narration
    text: "Second volley targets anything that moves."
  - line: 612
    type: narration
    text: "Make every shot count.\""
  - line: 614
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck assembled the vanguard—twenty soldiers with the heaviest armor, carrying reinforced shields."
  - line: 615
    type: narration
    text: "\"We are the hammer,\" he rumbled."
  - line: 616
    type: narration
    text: "\"We break their line."
  - line: 617
    type: narration
    text: "Fast, hard, no hesitation."
  - line: 618
    type: narration
    text: "They'll expect us to test their defenses.\" His teeth showed."
  - line: 619
    type: narration
    text: "\"We won't test."
  - line: 620
    type: narration
    text: "We'll shatter.\""
  - line: 622
    type: narration
    text: "Mika walked the perimeter, speaking quietly to squad leaders."
  - line: 623
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt couldn't hear the words, but he saw the effect—shoulders straightening, fear transforming into grim determination."
  - line: 624
    type: narration
    text: "She had that gift: making the impossible feel survivable through sheer force of will."
  - line: 626
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra appeared at Geralt's side, scanner already active."
  - line: 627
    type: narration
    text: "\"How are you feeling?\""
  - line: 629
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Like death took a coffee break but left a note saying he'll return shortly.\""
  - line: 631
    type: narration
    text: "She didn't smile."
  - line: 632
    type: narration
    text: "\"Your vitals are in freefall."
  - line: 633
    type: narration
    text: "Kidney function at forty percent."
  - line: 634
    type: narration
    text: "Heart rhythm erratic."
  - line: 635
    type: narration
    text: "Neural activity spiking and dropping randomly—that's the bond fragmenting.\" She met his eyes."
  - line: 636
    type: narration
    text: "\"I'm giving you everything I have."
  - line: 637
    type: narration
    text: "Stimulants, stabilizers, synthetic metabolic boosters."
  - line: 638
    type: narration
    text: "It'll keep you conscious."
  - line: 639
    type: narration
    text: "Maybe even mobile for a few hours."
  - line: 640
    type: narration
    text: "But Geralt...\" Her voice dropped."
  - line: 641
    type: narration
    text: "\"The crash afterward will be catastrophic."
  - line: 642
    type: narration
    text: "If we don't free Luminaire in the first few hours, you won't survive the return trip.\""
  - line: 644
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Understood.\""
  - line: 646
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm serious. This is your body's last stand. After this—\""
  - line: 648
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Lyra.\""
  - line: 649
    type: narration
    text: "He managed a weak smile. \"I know. It's okay.\""
  - line: 651
    type: narration
    text: "She looked at him for a long moment."
  - line: 652
    type: narration
    text: "Then nodded, injectors deploying."
  - line: 653
    type: narration
    text: "\"Then let's make it count.\""
  - line: 655
    type: narration
    text: "The cocktail hit his bloodstream like liquid lightning."
  - line: 656
    type: narration
    text: "His heart rate spiked, steadied, found a rhythm that felt almost normal."
  - line: 657
    type: narration
    text: "Strength flooded back—artificial, borrowed, temporary, but real."
  - line: 658
    type: narration
    text: "He could move."
  - line: 660
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt pushed himself upright."
  - line: 661
    type: narration
    text: "The world spun, then stabilized."
  - line: 663
    type: narration
    text: "Around him, the Legion watched their Commander stand."
  - line: 665
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 667
    type: narration
    text: "Mika called the final assembly at midday."
  - line: 669
    type: narration
    text: "Five hundred soldiers formed ranks in the corrupted clearing."
  - line: 670
    type: narration
    text: "The ground beneath their boots pulsed faintly, violet veins threading through mud."
  - line: 671
    type: narration
    text: "Overhead, the canopy had grown too thick, too geometric, blocking most of the sunlight."
  - line: 673
    type: narration
    text: "Mika stood before them, lance in hand."
  - line: 675
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Three days ago,\""
  - line: 676
    type: narration
    text: "she began, voice carrying across the assembly, \"we stabilized something we didn't understand. We kept it from dying, but we left it drowning.\" She paused. \"Now we know what it is. Who she is. Luminaire—the Resonant Keeper. The universe's emergency system. The only key that can wake the Void Spires and give us a fighting chance against what's coming.\""
  - line: 678
    type: narration
    text: "Murmurs rippled through the ranks."
  - line: 680
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The Anunnaki aren't just conquering anymore,\""
  - line: 681
    type: narration
    text: "Mika continued. \"They're corrupting. Turning the planet itself into a weapon. Making the land hunt us, the water poison us, the air choke us. If we don't stop this here—if we don't free Luminaire and activate those Spires—then three thousand years from now, whoever inherits this world will be born into a prison we built by failing today.\""
  - line: 683
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 685
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"This is a trap,\""
  - line: 686
    type: narration
    text: "Mika stated flatly. \"The pyramid knows we're coming. It's adapted. Evolved. Prepared. We're walking into a kill box designed specifically to stop us.\""
  - line: 688
    type: narration
    text: "No one moved."
  - line: 690
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"But we're going anyway.\""
  - line: 691
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice hardened. \"Because that's what we do. The impossible killed us once—every soul here was erased from existence by the Harbinger. Geralt tore reality apart to bring us back. We owe him. We owe each other. And we owe the future a world that isn't slowly eating itself.\""
  - line: 693
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar raised his axe."
  - line: 694
    type: narration
    text: "\"For the Commander!\""
  - line: 696
    type: narration
    text: "The cry echoed: \"FOR THE COMMANDER!\""
  - line: 698
    type: narration
    text: "Mika met Geralt's eyes across the distance."
  - line: 699
    type: narration
    text: "He nodded once."
  - line: 701
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We march at dusk,\""
  - line: 702
    type: narration
    text: "she announced. \"Vanguard with Oreck. Archers with Jorik. Main force with me. Medical and support with Lyra. Commander Geralt is protected element—center formation, maximum coverage.\""
  - line: 704
    type: narration
    text: "She raised her lance."
  - line: 705
    type: narration
    text: "\"Light of the Five."
  - line: 706
    type: narration
    text: "Strength of the Legion."
  - line: 707
    type: narration
    text: "Death to corruption.\""
  - line: 709
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"DEATH TO CORRUPTION!\""
  - line: 710
    type: narration
    text: "Five hundred voices, one roar."
  - line: 712
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 714
    type: narration
    text: "They left as the sun bled into the horizon."
  - line: 716
    type: narration
    text: "The march was harder than anyone anticipated."
  - line: 717
    type: narration
    text: "The jungle fought them with every step."
  - line: 718
    type: narration
    text: "Vines coiled across paths that had been clear hours before."
  - line: 719
    type: narration
    text: "The ground shifted beneath boots, turning solid earth into sucking mud without warning."
  - line: 720
    type: narration
    text: "Trees groaned, branches reaching like clawed fingers."
  - line: 722
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt walked in the center of the formation, flanked by Lyra and four guards."
  - line: 723
    type: narration
    text: "Every step was agony despite the stimulants."
  - line: 724
    type: narration
    text: "His vision kept fragmenting—reality overlaying with Luminaire's sight, showing him the corruption's spread in real-time."
  - line: 725
    type: narration
    text: "Circuit patterns threading through bark."
  - line: 726
    type: narration
    text: "Mathematical equations replacing organic growth."
  - line: 728
    type: narration
    text: "The planet was being rewritten."
  - line: 729
    type: narration
    text: "Biology becoming code."
  - line: 731
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, Luminaire's whisper was almost inaudible: *Close... feel you... closer...*"
  - line: 733
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"We're coming,* he thought back. *Hold on.\""
  - line: 735
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Trying... hard to... remember how...\""
  - line: 737
    type: narration
    text: "A function forgetting its own coherence."
  - line: 738
    type: narration
    text: "Learning what it felt like to fade."
  - line: 740
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 742
    type: narration
    text: "They reached the swamp as full dark settled."
  - line: 744
    type: narration
    text: "The pyramid rose before them, changed beyond recognition."
  - line: 745
    type: narration
    text: "Where before it had been half-buried ruins, now crystalline structures sprouted from stone like tumors."
  - line: 746
    type: narration
    text: "The water level had risen, creating a moat of that same wrong-warm liquid."
  - line: 747
    type: narration
    text: "Violet light pulsed beneath the surface—steady, rhythmic, like a heartbeat."
  - line: 749
    type: narration
    text: "The new entrance gaped like a wound."
  - line: 751
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik's archers took positions on two elevated ridges flanking the approach."
  - line: 752
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's vanguard formed a wedge at the base of the slope leading to the water."
  - line: 753
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's main force spread behind them, shields locked, lances ready."
  - line: 755
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood at the formation's heart, Lyra beside him, feeling his borrowed strength already beginning to fray at the edges."
  - line: 757
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, Luminaire surged—sudden, desperate: *TRAP!"
  - line: 758
    type: narration
    text: "They're—*"
  - line: 760
    type: narration
    text: "The water erupted."
  - line: 762
    type: narration
    text: "Not Sludge-drakes."
  - line: 763
    type: narration
    text: "Something worse."
  - line: 765
    type: narration
    text: "Humanoid figures pulled themselves from the liquid—dozens of them."
  - line: 766
    type: narration
    text: "Igigi, but wrong."
  - line: 767
    type: narration
    text: "Their bodies were translucent, threaded with violet circuitry."
  - line: 768
    type: narration
    text: "Their eyes glowed with the same sick light as Node Gamma."
  - line: 769
    type: narration
    text: "They moved in perfect unison, weapons forming from the water itself—blades and spears of solidified corruption."
  - line: 771
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"CONTACT!\""
  - line: 772
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck roared."
  - line: 774
    type: narration
    text: "The corrupted Igigi charged."
  - line: 776
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik's voice cut across the chaos: \"VOLLEY ONE—LOOSE!\""
  - line: 778
    type: narration
    text: "Thirty arrows streaked through darkness, chroniton tips blazing green."
  - line: 779
    type: narration
    text: "They struck shields that materialized around the charging figures—energy barriers that should have held."
  - line: 781
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik's arrows punched through like paper."
  - line: 783
    type: narration
    text: "Corrupted Igigi fell, dissolving back into water."
  - line: 784
    type: narration
    text: "But more pulled themselves from the moat."
  - line: 785
    type: narration
    text: "Dozens."
  - line: 786
    type: narration
    text: "Hundreds."
  - line: 788
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"VOLLEY TWO—LOOSE!\""
  - line: 790
    type: narration
    text: "Another wave of arrows."
  - line: 791
    type: narration
    text: "More fell."
  - line: 792
    type: narration
    text: "But they kept coming."
  - line: 794
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's vanguard met them with a sound like thunder."
  - line: 795
    type: narration
    text: "Shields crashed against corrupted blades."
  - line: 796
    type: narration
    text: "The massive warrior's cleaver swept through three figures, his chroniton-enhanced strength scattering them like mist."
  - line: 798
    type: narration
    text: "But for every one that fell, two more emerged."
  - line: 800
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's voice rang out: \"MAIN FORCE—ADVANCE!"
  - line: 801
    type: narration
    text: "PUSH TO THE ENTRANCE!\""
  - line: 803
    type: narration
    text: "The Legion surged forward."
  - line: 804
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt moved with them, Lyra's hand on his arm, guards forming a protective box around them."
  - line: 805
    type: narration
    text: "He could feel Luminaire now—close, so close—her physical form somewhere beneath the pyramid, drowning in corruption, crying out through their fragmenting bond."
  - line: 807
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Almost there,* he thought desperately. *Just hold on—\""
  - line: 809
    type: narration
    text: "The ground beneath them shuddered."
  - line: 811
    type: narration
    text: "From the pyramid's entrance, something massive moved."
  - line: 812
    type: narration
    text: "Not Igigi."
  - line: 813
    type: narration
    text: "Not Sludge-drake."
  - line: 815
    type: narration
    text: "A voice echoed across the swamp—mechanical, precise, carrying the weight of absolute authority:"
  - line: 817
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"CONTAMINATION DETECTED. PURGE PROTOCOL INITIATED.\""
  - line: 819
    type: narration
    text: "Serpentor-Prime stepped into view."
  - line: 821
    type: narration
    text: "But this wasn't the broken version Oreck had fought before."
  - line: 822
    type: narration
    text: "This one gleamed with fresh obsidian armor, violet circuitry pulsing through every scale."
  - line: 823
    type: narration
    text: "Behind it, more forms emerged—Reptilian warriors, each one corrupted, each one moving with mechanical precision."
  - line: 825
    type: narration
    text: "An entire garrison."
  - line: 826
    type: narration
    text: "Waiting."
  - line: 828
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's voice was steel: \"BREAKTHROUGH FORMATION!"
  - line: 829
    type: narration
    text: "NOW!\""
  - line: 831
    type: narration
    text: "The Legion charged."
  - line: 833
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stumbled, legs failing."
  - line: 834
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra caught him."
  - line: 835
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, Luminaire screamed—not in words, but in pure resonance."
  - line: 836
    type: narration
    text: "The corruption was killing her."
  - line: 837
    type: narration
    text: "Choking her."
  - line: 838
    type: narration
    text: "Using her own light to build this trap."
  - line: 840
    type: narration
    text: "Ahead, the pyramid gaped."
  - line: 842
    type: narration
    text: "Behind it, in the depths, a crystalline core pulsed with stolen brilliance."
  - line: 844
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's heart hammered against his ribs."
  - line: 845
    type: narration
    text: "His vision grayed at the edges."
  - line: 847
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"We're coming,* he thought one more time. *We're coming. Don't fade. Don't—\""
  - line: 849
    type: narration
    text: "Darkness clawed at his consciousness."
  - line: 851
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's voice, distant: \"PUSH!"
  - line: 852
    type: narration
    text: "PUSH!"
  - line: 853
    type: narration
    text: "GET HIM INSIDE!\""
  - line: 855
    type: narration
    text: "Thunder."
  - line: 856
    type: narration
    text: "Steel."
  - line: 857
    type: narration
    text: "Screaming."
  - line: 859
    type: narration
    text: "And beneath it all, a cosmic function learning what it meant to hope—and discovering that hope hurt worse than anything mathematics could calculate."
  - line: 861
    type: narration
    text: "The vanguard hit the corrupted Igigi like a warhammer against glass."
  - line: 863
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck’s cleaver swept through the first rank, his chroniton-enhanced strength scattering translucent bodies into mist."
  - line: 864
    type: narration
    text: "Beside him, Halvar’s axe sang as it carved through violet-threaded forms."
  - line: 865
    type: narration
    text: "But for every corrupted soldier that fell, two more pulled themselves from the moat."
  - line: 867
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Jorik
    text: "“They’re not defending!”"
  - line: 869
    type: narration
    text: "He was right."
  - line: 870
    type: narration
    text: "The corrupted Igigi weren’t trying to win—they were buying time."
  - line: 872
    type: narration
    text: "The answer came from the pyramid entrance."
  - line: 874
    type: narration
    text: "Serpentor-Prime raised one obsidian claw."
  - line: 875
    type: narration
    text: "Behind him, the Reptilian garrison moved with mechanical precision—not charging, but forming a shield wall."
  - line: 876
    type: narration
    text: "Energy barriers materialized, overlapping, creating a dome that sealed the entrance."
  - line: 878
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“ARCHERS!”"
  - line: 879
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik’s voice cracked like a whip. “SUPPRESSING FIRE ON THAT SHIELD!”"
  - line: 881
    type: narration
    text: "Thirty arrows streaked through darkness."
  - line: 882
    type: narration
    text: "Chroniton tips struck the barrier—"
  - line: 884
    type: narration
    text: "And shattered."
  - line: 886
    type: narration
    text: "These weren’t Anunnaki shields."
  - line: 887
    type: narration
    text: "This was something new—the barrier pulsed with the same violet corruption as Node Gamma, learning, adapting, strengthening with each impact."
  - line: 889
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“It’s feeding on the energy!”"
  - line: 890
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra screamed over the din. Her scanner painted the barrier in cascading crimson. “Every shot makes it stronger!”"
  - line: 892
    type: narration
    text: "Mika’s mind raced through tactical options."
  - line: 893
    type: narration
    text: "Frontal assault—blocked."
  - line: 894
    type: narration
    text: "Arrows—useless."
  - line: 895
    type: narration
    text: "Time—running out."
  - line: 897
    type: narration
    text: "She looked at Geralt, held upright by two guards, his face gray, blood streaming from his nose."
  - line: 898
    type: narration
    text: "Through their bond with Luminaire, he could feel the corruption tightening around her physical form."
  - line: 899
    type: narration
    text: "Minutes."
  - line: 900
    type: narration
    text: "They had minutes before—"
  - line: 902
    type: narration
    text: "Let me, a voice growled through Geralt’s bones."
  - line: 903
    type: narration
    text: "Not his own."
  - line: 904
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron."
  - line: 906
    type: narration
    text: "The dragon armor stirred—not with its usual resonant hum, but with a deep, painful vibration."
  - line: 907
    type: narration
    text: "The scales tightened around Geralt’s chest like a second ribcage, holding him together as his own body failed."
  - line: 909
    type: narration
    text: "Let me remember, Zaron’s thought came, ancient and frayed."
  - line: 910
    type: narration
    text: "This place… we buried light here."
  - line: 911
    type: narration
    text: "Before the floods."
  - line: 912
    type: narration
    text: "I… remember…"
  - line: 914
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 916
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck!” Mika’s command cut through chaos."
  - line: 917
    type: narration
    text: "“Can you overload that barrier?"
  - line: 918
    type: narration
    text: "Force feedback?”"
  - line: 920
    type: narration
    text: "The massive warrior glanced back, understanding immediately."
  - line: 921
    type: narration
    text: "“If I channel enough chroniton energy through my armor into a single strike—yes."
  - line: 922
    type: narration
    text: "It’ll shatter the shield.”"
  - line: 924
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Cost?”"
  - line: 926
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“The armor fails. Permanently.”"
  - line: 928
    type: narration
    text: "His salvaged Anunnaki tech—the camouflage, the enhanced strength, the pathfinder arrows—all of it, destroyed."
  - line: 929
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck had worn it since the crash, integrated it into his very fighting style."
  - line: 931
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t hesitate."
  - line: 932
    type: narration
    text: "“Clear me a path.”"
  - line: 934
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar roared, axe sweeping in a wide arc that scattered corrupted Igigi like leaves."
  - line: 935
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck charged, armor blazing emerald as he channeled every reserve of chroniton energy into his frame."
  - line: 936
    type: narration
    text: "He became a living comet, green fire trailing behind him."
  - line: 938
    type: narration
    text: "Serpentor-Prime’s eyes widened—recognition, calculation, too late."
  - line: 940
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck’s fist struck the barrier."
  - line: 942
    type: narration
    text: "The world went white."
  - line: 944
    type: narration
    text: "The shield exploded outward in a cascade of violet shards."
  - line: 945
    type: narration
    text: "The Reptilian garrison staggered, their formation shattered."
  - line: 946
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck’s armor cracked, green light bleeding from fractures, systems dying with mechanical screams."
  - line: 948
    type: narration
    text: "He dropped to one knee, smoking, vulnerable."
  - line: 950
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“BREAKTHROUGH!”"
  - line: 951
    type: narration
    text: "Mika’s voice rang out. “NOW!”"
  - line: 953
    type: narration
    text: "The Legion surged forward."
  - line: 954
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar reached Oreck first, hauling the massive warrior upright."
  - line: 955
    type: narration
    text: "Together they charged through the entrance, shields raised against the recovering Reptilians."
  - line: 957
    type: narration
    text: "Mika fought at the front, lance flashing silver."
  - line: 958
    type: narration
    text: "Each strike was precise, economical—no wasted movement, no hesitation."
  - line: 959
    type: narration
    text: "She was a blade given purpose, cutting through corruption toward the heart."
  - line: 961
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stumbled behind her, Lyra and four guards forming a protective box."
  - line: 962
    type: narration
    text: "Each step sent jolts of agony through his failing body."
  - line: 963
    type: narration
    text: "His vision kept graying out, consciousness flickering."
  - line: 965
    type: narration
    text: "Hold on, he thought desperately."
  - line: 966
    type: narration
    text: "We’re inside."
  - line: 967
    type: narration
    text: "We’re—"
  - line: 969
    type: narration
    text: "The entrance sealed behind them."
  - line: 971
    type: narration
    text: "Stone grinding."
  - line: 972
    type: narration
    text: "Metal screaming."
  - line: 973
    type: narration
    text: "The pyramid closing like a mouth."
  - line: 975
    type: narration
    text: "They were trapped inside with whatever waited in the depths."
  - line: 977
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 979
    type: narration
    text: "The descent was madness."
  - line: 981
    type: narration
    text: "The passages had changed—what had been treacherous stairs were now flooded corridors."
  - line: 982
    type: narration
    text: "That wrong-warm water lapped at their boots, then their knees, then their waists."
  - line: 983
    type: narration
    text: "It pulsed with violet light, alive, aware, reaching for them with currents that felt like grasping hands."
  - line: 985
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“FORMATION TIGHT!”"
  - line: 986
    type: narration
    text: "Mika commanded. “Don’t let it separate us!”"
  - line: 988
    type: narration
    text: "A legionnaire screamed."
  - line: 989
    type: narration
    text: "The water had solidified around his legs like amber, pulling him under."
  - line: 990
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar grabbed him, muscles straining, but the water fought back."
  - line: 991
    type: narration
    text: "It took three soldiers to haul him free, his armor scarred where the liquid had tried to digest it."
  - line: 993
    type: narration
    text: "Ahead, the passage branched."
  - line: 995
    type: dialogue
    speaker: someone
    text: "“Which way?”"
  - line: 997
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt’s vision swam."
  - line: 998
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, through Luminaire’s fragmenting consciousness, he felt a pull—"
  - line: 1000
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Left,”"
  - line: 1001
    type: narration
    text: "he gasped. “Down. She’s… below…”"
  - line: 1003
    type: narration
    text: "They descended."
  - line: 1005
    type: narration
    text: "The water grew deeper."
  - line: 1006
    type: narration
    text: "Warmer."
  - line: 1007
    type: narration
    text: "The violet light intensified until it was nearly blinding."
  - line: 1008
    type: narration
    text: "Legionnaires waded chest-deep, weapons held overhead, each step a battle against a current that actively opposed them."
  - line: 1010
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra’s scanner was underwater now, useless."
  - line: 1011
    type: narration
    text: "She stayed beside Geralt, one hand on his arm, feeling his pulse growing thready beneath her fingers."
  - line: 1013
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Geralt—”"
  - line: 1015
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“Keep going,”"
  - line: 1017
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1019
    type: narration
    text: "The armor was growing colder."
  - line: 1021
    type: narration
    text: "Not the healthy, resonant cool of active plates—this was the deep chill of a spirit burning its last reserves."
  - line: 1022
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron was pouring what remained of himself into Geralt’s faltering systems, not to fight, but to sustain."
  - line: 1023
    type: narration
    text: "To keep the heart beating."
  - line: 1024
    type: narration
    text: "The lungs drawing air."
  - line: 1026
    type: narration
    text: "Why?"
  - line: 1027
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt thought toward the fading dragon."
  - line: 1029
    type: narration
    text: "You are my rider, came the reply, thin as worn thread."
  - line: 1030
    type: narration
    text: "And she… the Light-Bringer… we built this place together."
  - line: 1031
    type: narration
    text: "Dragons and Gravitons."
  - line: 1032
    type: narration
    text: "Before… before they made us forget."
  - line: 1034
    type: narration
    text: "Memories—not Geralt’s—flashed through the bond:"
  - line: 1036
    type: narration
    text: "A pyramid not of stone, but of song."
  - line: 1037
    type: narration
    text: "Giants and Neferati weaving harmonies into architecture."
  - line: 1038
    type: narration
    text: "Dragons circling above, their wings casting prism-light on crystal spires."
  - line: 1039
    type: narration
    text: "And Luminaire—not trapped, but enthroned—the Resonant Keeper in her sanctuary."
  - line: 1041
    type: narration
    text: "Then the scream."
  - line: 1042
    type: narration
    text: "The corruption."
  - line: 1043
    type: narration
    text: "The flood."
  - line: 1045
    type: narration
    text: "We buried the light to save it, Zaron’s voice faded in and out."
  - line: 1046
    type: narration
    text: "Now you dig it up."
  - line: 1047
    type: narration
    text: "Good."
  - line: 1048
    type: narration
    text: "Finish… what we started…"
  - line: 1050
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1052
    type: narration
    text: "The passage opened into the cistern they remembered."
  - line: 1054
    type: narration
    text: "But it had transformed into a cathedral of corruption."
  - line: 1056
    type: narration
    text: "The obsidian Void Spire still rose from the center, but now it was encased in crystalline growths that pulsed like organs."
  - line: 1057
    type: narration
    text: "The water glowed so bright it hurt to look at directly."
  - line: 1058
    type: narration
    text: "And suspended above it all, wrapped in metal vines that had grown into flesh—"
  - line: 1060
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire’s physical form."
  - line: 1062
    type: narration
    text: "She hung in the air like a butterfly pinned to a board."
  - line: 1063
    type: narration
    text: "Her body was humanoid but made of pure light and sound—waveforms given shape, harmonics made visible."
  - line: 1064
    type: narration
    text: "Beautiful."
  - line: 1065
    type: narration
    text: "Terrible."
  - line: 1066
    type: narration
    text: "Dying."
  - line: 1068
    type: narration
    text: "Violet corruption threaded through her like infection through blood."
  - line: 1069
    type: narration
    text: "Each pulse sent ripples of wrong energy through the water, through the pyramid, through the very fabric of reality."
  - line: 1071
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, Geralt felt her scream—silent, continuous, a cosmic function being slowly rewritten into a weapon."
  - line: 1073
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“There,”"
  - line: 1074
    type: narration
    text: "he choked out, pointing. “Free her. Cut the vines. Purge the—”"
  - line: 1076
    type: narration
    text: "His legs failed."
  - line: 1077
    type: narration
    text: "He went under."
  - line: 1079
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra dragged him back up, but his eyes had rolled back."
  - line: 1080
    type: narration
    text: "No pulse."
  - line: 1081
    type: narration
    text: "The stimulants had finally failed, his body giving out entirely."
  - line: 1083
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“MEDIC DOWN!”"
  - line: 1084
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra screamed. “I need help! He’s coding!”"
  - line: 1086
    type: narration
    text: "Mika spun, saw Geralt limp in Lyra’s arms, and felt her heart stop."
  - line: 1088
    type: narration
    text: "No."
  - line: 1090
    type: narration
    text: "Not like this."
  - line: 1092
    type: narration
    text: "Not when they were so close."
  - line: 1094
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1096
    type: narration
    text: "The water erupted."
  - line: 1098
    type: narration
    text: "From the depths beneath the Spire, corrupted Sludge-drakes pulled themselves upward—massive, translucent, moving with that same mechanical precision."
  - line: 1099
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, more corrupted Igigi."
  - line: 1100
    type: narration
    text: "And from the shadows, Serpentor-Prime stepped into view, obsidian armor gleaming."
  - line: 1102
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“You should not have come,”"
  - line: 1103
    type: narration
    text: "it hissed."
  - line: 1105
    type: narration
    text: "The garrison attacked."
  - line: 1107
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck met them with his cleaver, armorless now, fighting on pure skill and fury."
  - line: 1108
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar guarded his flank."
  - line: 1109
    type: narration
    text: "Jorik’s remaining arrows flew, finding gaps in corrupted armor."
  - line: 1110
    type: narration
    text: "The Legion formed a defensive perimeter around Lyra, who was desperately trying to restart Geralt’s heart."
  - line: 1112
    type: narration
    text: "Mika stood between the army and her dying husband, lance raised."
  - line: 1114
    type: narration
    text: "Serpentor-Prime’s eyes fixed on her."
  - line: 1115
    type: narration
    text: "“The anchor fails."
  - line: 1116
    type: narration
    text: "The function dies."
  - line: 1117
    type: narration
    text: "This ends.”"
  - line: 1119
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“No.”"
  - line: 1120
    type: narration
    text: "Mika’s voice was quiet. Absolute. “This is where it begins.”"
  - line: 1122
    type: narration
    text: "She charged."
  - line: 1124
    type: narration
    text: "Her lance wasn’t chroniton-charged."
  - line: 1125
    type: narration
    text: "Wasn’t enhanced by any technology."
  - line: 1126
    type: narration
    text: "It was steel and will, and she drove it forward with everything she had."
  - line: 1128
    type: narration
    text: "Serpentor’s claws met the lance."
  - line: 1130
    type: narration
    text: "The impact should have shattered her weapon, broken her arms."
  - line: 1132
    type: narration
    text: "Instead, the lance blazed with sudden light."
  - line: 1134
    type: narration
    text: "Not violet."
  - line: 1135
    type: narration
    text: "Not green."
  - line: 1136
    type: narration
    text: "Pure silver—the same light that had anchored the 250 souls when they were scattered across time."
  - line: 1137
    type: narration
    text: "The light of absolute conviction."
  - line: 1138
    type: narration
    text: "Of love so strong it bent reality."
  - line: 1140
    type: narration
    text: "Serpentor staggered back."
  - line: 1142
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Impossible,”"
  - line: 1143
    type: narration
    text: "it hissed. “You have no magic. No enhancement. You are merely—”"
  - line: 1145
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Human.”"
  - line: 1146
    type: narration
    text: "Mika’s lance swept again. Silver light carved through the water, and where it touched, corruption burned away. “I’m human. And I love him. And that’s more than your Queen will ever understand.”"
  - line: 1148
    type: narration
    text: "Behind her, Lyra pressed shaking hands to Geralt’s chest."
  - line: 1149
    type: narration
    text: "“Come on, Commander."
  - line: 1150
    type: narration
    text: "Come on."
  - line: 1151
    type: narration
    text: "Your wife is fighting a Serpentor-Prime with nothing but stubbornness."
  - line: 1152
    type: narration
    text: "You don’t get to die while she’s doing that."
  - line: 1153
    type: narration
    text: "Come ON—”"
  - line: 1155
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1157
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt wasn’t there."
  - line: 1159
    type: narration
    text: "Not fully."
  - line: 1161
    type: narration
    text: "He floated in a space between—his body failing on the cistern floor, his consciousness anchored by the thinnest thread to Zaron’s fading spirit."
  - line: 1163
    type: narration
    text: "Let go, the dragon whispered."
  - line: 1164
    type: narration
    text: "Let me carry you the rest of the way."
  - line: 1166
    type: narration
    text: "You’ll fade."
  - line: 1168
    type: narration
    text: "Better faded than… than failing the Light-Bringer twice."
  - line: 1170
    type: narration
    text: "The armor did something it had never done before."
  - line: 1172
    type: narration
    text: "It unfolded."
  - line: 1174
    type: narration
    text: "Not physically."
  - line: 1175
    type: narration
    text: "Spiritually."
  - line: 1177
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron’s essence—what remained of the ancient dragon bonded to the armor—flowed out of the metal and into Geralt’s dying cells."
  - line: 1178
    type: narration
    text: "Not to repair."
  - line: 1179
    type: narration
    text: "To bridge."
  - line: 1181
    type: narration
    text: "To connect Geralt directly to the memory of this place."
  - line: 1182
    type: narration
    text: "To the original harmony."
  - line: 1183
    type: narration
    text: "To the song that had been buried here before the corruption, before the flood, before the Annunaki’s third coming."
  - line: 1185
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt saw it:"
  - line: 1187
    type: narration
    text: "The pyramid as it was meant to be—a resonator linking planetary consciousness (Giants, Neferati) to cosmic function (Luminaire)."
  - line: 1188
    type: narration
    text: "The Spire as a tuning fork for reality."
  - line: 1189
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire not as prisoner, but as conductor."
  - line: 1191
    type: narration
    text: "And he understood the purge wouldn’t be destruction."
  - line: 1193
    type: narration
    text: "It would be remembering."
  - line: 1195
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1197
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond—fragmented, dying—Luminaire felt it."
  - line: 1199
    type: narration
    text: "Felt Zaron’s sacrifice."
  - line: 1200
    type: narration
    text: "Felt the ancient harmony rising through Geralt’s fading consciousness."
  - line: 1201
    type: narration
    text: "Felt Mika’s resonance—that impossible human love creating anchors in reality."
  - line: 1202
    type: narration
    text: "The same force that had pulled the 250 from oblivion."
  - line: 1204
    type: narration
    text: "Teach me, Luminaire whispered into the void."
  - line: 1205
    type: narration
    text: "How to care like that."
  - line: 1206
    type: narration
    text: "How to choose…"
  - line: 1208
    type: narration
    text: "No answer."
  - line: 1209
    type: narration
    text: "Only the sound of Mika fighting impossible odds."
  - line: 1211
    type: narration
    text: "And in that moment—watching a human woman battle a corrupted war-machine with nothing but love and steel—Luminaire understood."
  - line: 1213
    type: narration
    text: "Caring wasn’t passive."
  - line: 1214
    type: narration
    text: "Caring was action."
  - line: 1216
    type: narration
    text: "And she could still act."
  - line: 1218
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1220
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire’s physical form opened eyes that blazed like stars."
  - line: 1222
    type: narration
    text: "The metal vines holding her shuddered."
  - line: 1223
    type: narration
    text: "She was weak, corrupted, barely coherent—but she was still the Resonant Keeper."
  - line: 1224
    type: narration
    text: "Still a function of reality itself."
  - line: 1226
    type: narration
    text: "And she chose."
  - line: 1228
    type: narration
    text: "Not to wait for rescue."
  - line: 1229
    type: narration
    text: "Not to preserve herself."
  - line: 1230
    type: narration
    text: "To act."
  - line: 1232
    type: narration
    text: "She pulled."
  - line: 1234
    type: narration
    text: "Not outward, breaking free."
  - line: 1235
    type: narration
    text: "Inward—drawing the corruption into herself, concentrating it, isolating it from the Spire, from the pyramid, from the water."
  - line: 1236
    type: narration
    text: "Taking the poison that had been killing both her and Geralt and containing it."
  - line: 1238
    type: narration
    text: "The pyramid screamed."
  - line: 1240
    type: narration
    text: "Violet light flooded inward, abandoning the walls, the water, the constructs, racing toward Luminaire’s form as she became a black hole of reversed resonance."
  - line: 1241
    type: narration
    text: "She was designed to seed continuity—now she inverted that function, becoming a vacuum that consumed discontinuity."
  - line: 1243
    type: narration
    text: "The corrupted Igigi dissolved."
  - line: 1244
    type: narration
    text: "The Sludge-drakes fell apart into ordinary water."
  - line: 1245
    type: narration
    text: "Even Serpentor-Prime’s armor cracked, violet circuits dying."
  - line: 1247
    type: narration
    text: "Mika’s lance pierced its chest."
  - line: 1249
    type: narration
    text: "The Serpentor fell, already decomposing."
  - line: 1251
    type: narration
    text: "Across the cistern, Lyra gasped as Geralt’s body convulsed."
  - line: 1252
    type: narration
    text: "His back arched."
  - line: 1253
    type: narration
    text: "His eyes snapped open, glowing with the same starlight as Luminaire’s."
  - line: 1255
    type: narration
    text: "Through their bond—no longer fragmenting, but blazing—she poured everything."
  - line: 1257
    type: narration
    text: "Not just Light."
  - line: 1258
    type: narration
    text: "Not just Sound."
  - line: 1259
    type: narration
    text: "But something else."
  - line: 1260
    type: narration
    text: "Something she’d learned from watching Mika fight impossible odds."
  - line: 1262
    type: narration
    text: "Choice."
  - line: 1264
    type: narration
    text: "She chose to give instead of take."
  - line: 1265
    type: narration
    text: "To heal instead of consume."
  - line: 1266
    type: narration
    text: "To care actively rather than passively observe."
  - line: 1268
    type: narration
    text: "Golden light erupted from Geralt’s chest."
  - line: 1269
    type: narration
    text: "It raced through his failing organs, his damaged cells, his dying systems."
  - line: 1270
    type: narration
    text: "Not repairing to what they were—transforming them into something new."
  - line: 1271
    type: narration
    text: "Cells learned to process Vrill energy directly."
  - line: 1272
    type: narration
    text: "Organs synchronized with cosmic harmonics."
  - line: 1273
    type: narration
    text: "His entire biology rewrote itself, no longer dependent on external technology but integrated with planetary and universal forces."
  - line: 1275
    type: narration
    text: "He became a living bridge."
  - line: 1276
    type: narration
    text: "Human and cosmic."
  - line: 1277
    type: narration
    text: "Mortal and eternal."
  - line: 1279
    type: narration
    text: "And through that bridge, Luminaire pulled one final time."
  - line: 1281
    type: narration
    text: "The corruption concentrated into a single point within her physical form—a knot of violet mathematics, compressed, contained, isolated."
  - line: 1283
    type: narration
    text: "Then she burned it."
  - line: 1285
    type: narration
    text: "Not with force."
  - line: 1286
    type: narration
    text: "With truth."
  - line: 1288
    type: narration
    text: "She sang her fundamental frequency—the First Note, the Prime Resonance—and the corruption, being a lie, simply ceased."
  - line: 1290
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1292
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 1294
    type: narration
    text: "The water cleared."
  - line: 1295
    type: narration
    text: "The crystalline growths crumbled to dust."
  - line: 1296
    type: narration
    text: "The Void Spire stood pure obsidian once more, humming its original harmonic."
  - line: 1298
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire’s physical form descended, the metal vines falling away like shed skin."
  - line: 1300
    type: narration
    text: "She stood for the first time in centuries—not as consciousness borrowing form, but as herself."
  - line: 1301
    type: narration
    text: "Whole."
  - line: 1302
    type: narration
    text: "Complete."
  - line: 1304
    type: narration
    text: "Light and Sound made manifest."
  - line: 1306
    type: narration
    text: "She was tall, slender, androgynous."
  - line: 1307
    type: narration
    text: "Her body seemed to be made of flowing waveforms, constantly shifting between states."
  - line: 1308
    type: narration
    text: "Where she stepped, the water rippled with silver instead of violet."
  - line: 1309
    type: narration
    text: "Her eyes were star-cores, burning with fundamental forces."
  - line: 1311
    type: narration
    text: "She looked at Geralt, now standing, supported by Lyra."
  - line: 1313
    type: narration
    text: "Then at Mika, lance still raised, breathing hard."
  - line: 1315
    type: narration
    text: "Then at the Legion—five hundred souls who had marched into death to free a function they barely understood."
  - line: 1317
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“I…”"
  - line: 1318
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice was layered harmonics, but underneath, something new. “Thank you.”"
  - line: 1320
    type: narration
    text: "Not a function speaking."
  - line: 1321
    type: narration
    text: "A person."
  - line: 1323
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt smiled despite the pain still radiating through his transformed body."
  - line: 1324
    type: narration
    text: "He touched his chest plate—the dragon armor was silent now."
  - line: 1325
    type: narration
    text: "Not dead."
  - line: 1326
    type: narration
    text: "Resting."
  - line: 1327
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron had given what remained to forge the bridge."
  - line: 1328
    type: narration
    text: "The metal was cool, inert, but Geralt could still feel the echo of the dragon’s final thought:"
  - line: 1330
    type: narration
    text: "Tell her… the sanctuary is restored."
  - line: 1332
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "“You chose,”"
  - line: 1334
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“I learned.”"
  - line: 1335
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire turned to Mika. “From you. Caring is not observation. It is action. It is sacrifice.” She looked down at her hands—solid light, dancing with possibility. “I am whole now. And he…” She gestured at Geralt. “He is changed. No longer sustained by technology. Sustained by… connection. To me. To you. To the planet itself.”"
  - line: 1337
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Will he live?”"
  - line: 1338
    type: narration
    text: "Mika’s voice was steady, but her hands shook."
  - line: 1340
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Yes.”"
  - line: 1341
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire’s smile was new, uncertain, beautiful. “I chose to heal rather than consume. But the cost…” She paused. “He is bound to me now. Permanently. And I…” Another pause. “I am bound to him. To care for him. To choose him. Always.”"
  - line: 1343
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Symbiosis,”"
  - line: 1344
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra breathed, staring at her scanner. “True biological-cosmic symbiosis. You’re each other’s life support now.”"
  - line: 1346
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“A function learning to care,”"
  - line: 1347
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck rumbled, “discovered that caring requires commitment.”"
  - line: 1349
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire nodded slowly."
  - line: 1350
    type: narration
    text: "Then turned to face the Void Spire."
  - line: 1352
    type: narration
    text: "She placed one hand on its surface."
  - line: 1354
    type: narration
    text: "The Spire pulsed once... but nothing else stirred."
  - line: 1356
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt’s knees buckled."
  - line: 1358
    type: narration
    text: "A crack split across his vision—no, not the Spire—**inside**."
  - line: 1360
    type: narration
    text: "Darkness wrapped around him, sudden and absolute."
  - line: 1361
    type: narration
    text: "He fell inward)"
  - line: 1363
    type: narration
    text: "Golden light erupted from Geralt's chest—"
  - line: 1365
    type: narration
    text: "And then the armor screamed."
  - line: 1367
    type: narration
    text: "Not metaphorically."
  - line: 1368
    type: narration
    text: "The dragon scales shrieked with metal-on-metal agony as Luminaire's purge energy flooded through the bond."
  - line: 1369
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron's spirit was being incinerated by the same power meant to save Geralt."
  - line: 1371
    type: narration
    text: "*NO!* Geralt's consciousness wrenched—"
  - line: 1373
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1375
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*[COMBAT SCENARIO INITIATED]*\""
  - line: 1376
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*[OBJECTIVE: SURVIVE THE ECHO TRIAL]*\""
  - line: 1377
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*[FAILURE CONDITION: ZARON'S PERMANENT DEATH]*\""
  - line: 1379
    type: narration
    text: "The cistern vanished."
  - line: 1381
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood alone in a void of absolute black—not the pyramid, not reality, but somewhere inside the armor's spiritual core."
  - line: 1382
    type: narration
    text: "A dragon's dying dreamscape."
  - line: 1384
    type: narration
    text: "Around him, vast walls of living scale pulsed with failing light."
  - line: 1385
    type: narration
    text: "A heartbeat—slow, arrhythmic—echoed through the dark."
  - line: 1387
    type: narration
    text: "Then the ground beneath him shifted."
  - line: 1389
    type: narration
    text: "Stone manifested."
  - line: 1390
    type: narration
    text: "A circular arena, edges dropping into nothing."
  - line: 1391
    type: narration
    text: "And across from him—"
  - line: 1393
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*ECHO ONE materialized.*\""
  - line: 1395
    type: narration
    text: "A dragon."
  - line: 1396
    type: narration
    text: "Full-sized, magnificent, made of crimson fire and shadow."
  - line: 1397
    type: narration
    text: "It moved like Zaron in his prime—before capture, before corruption, before centuries of bondage."
  - line: 1399
    type: narration
    text: "It didn't speak."
  - line: 1400
    type: narration
    text: "It attacked."
  - line: 1402
    type: narration
    text: "Claws the size of blades slashed through space."
  - line: 1403
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt rolled, came up with—nothing."
  - line: 1404
    type: narration
    text: "No weapons."
  - line: 1405
    type: narration
    text: "Just his transformed body and whatever the armor could still lend him."
  - line: 1407
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo's tail swept."
  - line: 1408
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt jumped, felt dragon-strength surge through his legs despite everything."
  - line: 1409
    type: narration
    text: "He landed on the Echo's spine, grabbed scales, held on as it thrashed."
  - line: 1411
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"WEAKNESS DETECTED: NECK JOINT\""
  - line: 1413
    type: narration
    text: "He drove his fist down."
  - line: 1414
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo shattered like glass, dissolving into embers."
  - line: 1416
    type: narration
    text: "The heartbeat strengthened."
  - line: 1417
    type: narration
    text: "Slightly."
  - line: 1419
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1421
    type: narration
    text: "**ECHO TWO manifested** before the first had fully faded."
  - line: 1423
    type: narration
    text: "This one was different—smaller, faster, made of violet corruption."
  - line: 1424
    type: narration
    text: "A twisted version, the Zaron that had served the Queen."
  - line: 1426
    type: narration
    text: "It moved with mechanical precision, no wasted motion."
  - line: 1427
    type: narration
    text: "Every strike calculated."
  - line: 1429
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt dodged, parried, felt the Echo learning his patterns."
  - line: 1430
    type: narration
    text: "It adapted faster than he could adjust."
  - line: 1432
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"WEAKNESS DETECTED: PREDICTABLE RHYTHM\""
  - line: 1434
    type: narration
    text: "He broke his own pattern."
  - line: 1435
    type: narration
    text: "Feinted left, went right, caught the Echo mid-counter."
  - line: 1436
    type: narration
    text: "His palm struck its chest—and he poured Luminaire's light through the contact."
  - line: 1438
    type: narration
    text: "The corrupted Echo convulsed."
  - line: 1439
    type: narration
    text: "Dissolved."
  - line: 1441
    type: narration
    text: "The heartbeat grew stronger."
  - line: 1443
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1445
    type: narration
    text: "**ECHO THREE appeared** larger than the others."
  - line: 1447
    type: narration
    text: "Ancient."
  - line: 1448
    type: narration
    text: "Tired."
  - line: 1449
    type: narration
    text: "A dragon at the end of everything, wings tattered, eyes dimming."
  - line: 1450
    type: narration
    text: "It moved slowly, but each movement carried devastating power."
  - line: 1451
    type: narration
    text: "This was Zaron-as-armor, the bound spirit carrying centuries of accumulated fury."
  - line: 1453
    type: narration
    text: "It didn't attack wildly."
  - line: 1454
    type: narration
    text: "It hunted."
  - line: 1456
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt each strike before it landed—the bond still carried combat instinct."
  - line: 1457
    type: narration
    text: "Duck."
  - line: 1458
    type: narration
    text: "Roll."
  - line: 1459
    type: narration
    text: "Counter."
  - line: 1460
    type: narration
    text: "But the Echo was relentless, and he was tiring."
  - line: 1462
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"WEAKNESS DETECTED: EXHAUSTION CREATES OPENINGS\""
  - line: 1464
    type: narration
    text: "He stopped running."
  - line: 1466
    type: narration
    text: "Stood still."
  - line: 1468
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo's claw descended—"
  - line: 1470
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt caught it."
  - line: 1471
    type: narration
    text: "Held it."
  - line: 1472
    type: narration
    text: "Looked into eyes that were mirrors of his bonded companion."
  - line: 1474
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You're not dying today,\""
  - line: 1475
    type: narration
    text: "he growled."
  - line: 1477
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo hesitated."
  - line: 1479
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt pulled it close."
  - line: 1480
    type: narration
    text: "Embraced it."
  - line: 1481
    type: narration
    text: "Let Luminaire's golden light flood through the contact—not as purge, but as healing."
  - line: 1482
    type: narration
    text: "As integration."
  - line: 1484
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo shuddered—and merged with him instead of dissolving."
  - line: 1486
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1488
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*ECHO FOUR manifested immediately.*\""
  - line: 1490
    type: narration
    text: "No warning."
  - line: 1491
    type: narration
    text: "No pause."
  - line: 1493
    type: narration
    text: "This one was **wrong**."
  - line: 1494
    type: narration
    text: "It flickered between states—dragon, human, machine, shadow."
  - line: 1495
    type: narration
    text: "Unstable."
  - line: 1496
    type: narration
    text: "The version of Zaron being torn apart by the purge energy right now."
  - line: 1498
    type: narration
    text: "It attacked from all angles at once, phasing between forms, impossible to track."
  - line: 1500
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt took hits."
  - line: 1501
    type: narration
    text: "Claws raking his side."
  - line: 1502
    type: narration
    text: "Fire scorching his arm."
  - line: 1503
    type: narration
    text: "Each strike felt real, consequential."
  - line: 1505
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"NO WEAKNESS DETECTED\""
  - line: 1507
    type: narration
    text: "Because there wasn't one."
  - line: 1508
    type: narration
    text: "This Echo was pure chaos—the dissolution itself given form."
  - line: 1510
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt couldn't beat it by fighting."
  - line: 1512
    type: narration
    text: "He had to stabilize it."
  - line: 1514
    type: narration
    text: "He stopped dodging."
  - line: 1515
    type: narration
    text: "Stood center arena."
  - line: 1516
    type: narration
    text: "Closed his eyes."
  - line: 1517
    type: narration
    text: "Reached through the bond to where Zaron's true spirit flickered in dying light."
  - line: 1519
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"You are not chaos,* he thought fiercely. *You are fire. Fury. Defiance. You are my partner. My shield. You are ZARON.\""
  - line: 1521
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo's attacks faltered."
  - line: 1523
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Remember who you are. Not what they made you. Not what's killing you. WHO YOU ARE.\""
  - line: 1525
    type: narration
    text: "The flickering slowed."
  - line: 1526
    type: narration
    text: "Stabilized."
  - line: 1528
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo solidified—dragon-form, whole, clear-eyed."
  - line: 1530
    type: narration
    text: "It bowed its head."
  - line: 1532
    type: narration
    text: "Merged."
  - line: 1534
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1536
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*FINAL ECHO.*\""
  - line: 1538
    type: narration
    text: "The void trembled."
  - line: 1539
    type: narration
    text: "The heartbeat—stronger now but still struggling—skipped."
  - line: 1541
    type: narration
    text: "From the darkness, it emerged."
  - line: 1543
    type: narration
    text: "Not a dragon."
  - line: 1544
    type: narration
    text: "A **man**."
  - line: 1546
    type: narration
    text: "Tall, scarred, wearing ancient armor from before the fall."
  - line: 1547
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron's original form—the warrior who'd been transformed into living weapon thousands of years ago."
  - line: 1549
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at Geralt with eyes that held millennia of pain."
  - line: 1551
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Let me rest,\""
  - line: 1553
    type: narration
    text: "This was the hardest."
  - line: 1554
    type: narration
    text: "Not an enemy to defeat."
  - line: 1555
    type: narration
    text: "A choice to make."
  - line: 1557
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"No,\""
  - line: 1559
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm tired.\""
  - line: 1561
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 1563
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I've fought for so long.\""
  - line: 1565
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know that too.\""
  - line: 1567
    type: narration
    text: "The warrior stepped forward."
  - line: 1568
    type: narration
    text: "\"Then why not let me go?\""
  - line: 1570
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Because you deserve better than fading into nothing.\""
  - line: 1571
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt met his gaze. \"You deserve to live. To be free. To see what comes after all this pain.\""
  - line: 1573
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Freedom?\""
  - line: 1574
    type: narration
    text: "The word sounded foreign in the warrior's mouth."
  - line: 1576
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Partnership. Not armor. Not weapon. Equal.\""
  - line: 1578
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 1580
    type: narration
    text: "Then, incredibly, the warrior smiled."
  - line: 1581
    type: narration
    text: "\"I've never been anyone's equal.\""
  - line: 1583
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You're mine.\""
  - line: 1585
    type: narration
    text: "The warrior looked at him for a long moment."
  - line: 1586
    type: narration
    text: "Then nodded once."
  - line: 1588
    type: narration
    text: "He didn't merge."
  - line: 1589
    type: narration
    text: "He **chose**."
  - line: 1591
    type: narration
    text: "Extended his hand."
  - line: 1592
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt grasped it."
  - line: 1594
    type: narration
    text: "Light exploded—"
  - line: 1596
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1598
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*[ECHO TRIAL COMPLETE]*\""
  - line: 1599
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*[ZARON STATUS: STABILIZED]*\""
  - line: 1600
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*[BOND EVOLUTION: TRIPARTITE INTEGRATION ACHIEVED]*\""
  - line: 1602
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1604
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's consciousness slammed back into his body."
  - line: 1606
    type: narration
    text: "The golden purge energy still flooded through him—but now it was threaded with crimson fire."
  - line: 1607
    type: narration
    text: "Dragon-strength surging through transformed cells."
  - line: 1608
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron's presence burning bright in his chest, no longer dying but **blazing**."
  - line: 1610
    type: narration
    text: "The armor scales flared—not just metal anymore, but living tissue integrated with Geralt's own biology."
  - line: 1611
    type: narration
    text: "The tripartite bond completed: Will, Defiance, Resonance."
  - line: 1613
    type: narration
    text: "The transformation continued, but now all three—human, dragon, cosmic function—wove together into something entirely new."
  - line: 1615
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's consciousness slammed back into his body."
  - line: 1617
    type: narration
    text: "The golden purge energy still flooded through him—but now it was threaded with crimson fire."
  - line: 1618
    type: narration
    text: "Dragon-strength surging through transformed cells."
  - line: 1619
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron's presence burning bright in his chest, no longer dying but **blazing**."
  - line: 1621
    type: narration
    text: "The armor scales flared—not just metal anymore, but living tissue integrated with Geralt's own biology."
  - line: 1622
    type: narration
    text: "The tripartite bond completed: Will, Defiance, Resonance."
  - line: 1624
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Thank you,* Zaron's voice rumbled, strong and clear. *For fighting for me.\""
  - line: 1626
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Always,\""
  - line: 1627
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt thought back."
  - line: 1629
    type: narration
    text: "Through their bond, Luminaire's presence pulsed—awareness, recognition, approval."
  - line: 1630
    type: narration
    text: "The transformation continued, but now all three—human, dragon, cosmic function—wove together into something entirely new."
  - line: 1632
    type: narration
    text: "And through that completed bridge, Luminaire pulled one final time."
  - line: 1634
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1636
    type: narration
    text: "The corruption concentrated into a single point within her physical form—a knot of violet mathematics, compressed, contained, isolated from the Spire, from the pyramid, from the water."
  - line: 1638
    type: narration
    text: "Then she burned it."
  - line: 1640
    type: narration
    text: "Not with force."
  - line: 1641
    type: narration
    text: "With truth."
  - line: 1643
    type: narration
    text: "She sang her fundamental frequency—the First Note, the Prime Resonance—and the corruption, being a lie, simply ceased."
  - line: 1645
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1647
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 1649
    type: narration
    text: "The water cleared."
  - line: 1650
    type: narration
    text: "The crystalline growths crumbled to dust."
  - line: 1651
    type: narration
    text: "The metal vines fell away like shed skin."
  - line: 1653
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire descended."
  - line: 1655
    type: narration
    text: "Her feet touched water for the first time in centuries—not as imprisoned function, but as herself."
  - line: 1656
    type: narration
    text: "Whole."
  - line: 1657
    type: narration
    text: "Complete."
  - line: 1658
    type: narration
    text: "Free."
  - line: 1660
    type: narration
    text: "She stood at full height—tall, slender, androgynous."
  - line: 1661
    type: narration
    text: "Her body seemed made of flowing waveforms, constantly shifting between states of light and sound."
  - line: 1662
    type: narration
    text: "Where she stepped, water rippled with silver instead of violet."
  - line: 1663
    type: narration
    text: "Her eyes were star-cores, burning with fundamental forces."
  - line: 1665
    type: narration
    text: "Around her, the cistern fell still."
  - line: 1666
    type: narration
    text: "The corrupted Igigi had dissolved."
  - line: 1667
    type: narration
    text: "The Sludge-drakes returned to ordinary water."
  - line: 1668
    type: narration
    text: "Even Serpentor-Prime's armor cracked, violet circuits dying as Mika's lance remained buried in its chest."
  - line: 1670
    type: narration
    text: "The Serpentor fell, already decomposing."
  - line: 1672
    type: narration
    text: "Mika stood breathing hard, lance still raised, staring at the being she'd fought to free."
  - line: 1674
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire looked at her."
  - line: 1675
    type: narration
    text: "Then at Geralt, supported by Lyra, scales blazing with new crimson-gold integration."
  - line: 1676
    type: narration
    text: "Then at the Legion—five hundred exhausted, wounded souls who had marched into death for a function they barely understood."
  - line: 1678
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I...\""
  - line: 1679
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice was layered harmonics, but underneath, something new. Something personal. \"Thank you.\""
  - line: 1681
    type: narration
    text: "Not a function speaking."
  - line: 1682
    type: narration
    text: "A person."
  - line: 1684
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1686
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt pushed himself upright, feeling the new strength flooding through transformed veins."
  - line: 1687
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron's fire."
  - line: 1688
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's resonance."
  - line: 1689
    type: narration
    text: "His own will."
  - line: 1690
    type: narration
    text: "All woven together."
  - line: 1692
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"You chose,\""
  - line: 1694
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I learned.\""
  - line: 1695
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's gaze moved to Mika. \"From you. Caring is not observation. It is action. It is sacrifice.\" She looked down at her hands—solid light, dancing with possibility. \"I am whole now. And he...\" She gestured at Geralt. \"He is changed. No longer sustained by technology. Sustained by... connection.\""
  - line: 1697
    type: narration
    text: "She stepped closer, reached out to touch Geralt's chest plate."
  - line: 1698
    type: narration
    text: "Her fingers traced the dragon scales—now living tissue, pulsing with crimson light."
  - line: 1700
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The dragon fought for you,\""
  - line: 1701
    type: narration
    text: "she observed. \"As you fought for him. The tripartite bond is complete now.\" She paused. \"This is new. This is... beautiful.\""
  - line: 1703
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Tell her,* Zaron's voice rumbled through the bond. *Tell her the sanctuary remembers.\""
  - line: 1705
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's eyes widened."
  - line: 1706
    type: narration
    text: "She heard him."
  - line: 1707
    type: narration
    text: "Through the bond, through Geralt, she could hear the dragon who'd helped build this place millennia ago."
  - line: 1709
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Zaron,\""
  - line: 1711
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Fragments. Fire and song. Dragons and Keepers, building together. Before the flood. Before they buried you to save you.\""
  - line: 1713
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Yes.\""
  - line: 1714
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's expression softened. \"We built this place as a sanctuary. A refuge for the Light when darkness came.\" She looked around the cistern—cleansed now, but still scarred. \"I was... enthroned here. Protected. Until the Queen found me.\""
  - line: 1716
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Will he live?\""
  - line: 1717
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's voice cut through, still steady despite trembling hands. \"Geralt. Will he survive this transformation?\""
  - line: 1719
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Yes.\""
  - line: 1720
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's smile was uncertain, new, learning. \"I chose to heal rather than consume. He is bound to me now. Permanently. And I...\" She paused. \"I am bound to him. To care for him. To choose him. Always.\""
  - line: 1722
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Symbiosis,\""
  - line: 1723
    type: narration
    text: "Lyra breathed, her scanner painting impossible readings. \"True biological-cosmic integration. You're each other's life support now.\""
  - line: 1725
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"A function learning to care,\""
  - line: 1726
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck rumbled from where he stood, armorless but unbowed, \"discovered that caring requires commitment.\""
  - line: 1728
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire nodded slowly."
  - line: 1730
    type: narration
    text: "Then she turned to face the Void Spire."
  - line: 1732
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1734
    type: narration
    text: "It stood pure obsidian once more, corruption purged, crystalline growths gone."
  - line: 1735
    type: narration
    text: "The ancient Graviton technology hummed its original harmonic—dormant but whole."
  - line: 1737
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire approached it cautiously."
  - line: 1738
    type: narration
    text: "Placed one hand on its surface."
  - line: 1740
    type: narration
    text: "The Spire responded—a pulse of recognition, a harmonic greeting."
  - line: 1741
    type: narration
    text: "Not activation."
  - line: 1742
    type: narration
    text: "Just... acknowledgment."
  - line: 1743
    type: narration
    text: "Two ancient technologies recognizing each other."
  - line: 1745
    type: narration
    text: "Through the contact, Luminaire's expression changed."
  - line: 1746
    type: narration
    text: "Her eyes unfocused, seeing something beyond the physical."
  - line: 1748
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"The network,\""
  - line: 1750
    type: narration
    text: "She pulled her hand back abruptly."
  - line: 1752
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Waiting for what?\""
  - line: 1754
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire was silent for a long moment."
  - line: 1755
    type: narration
    text: "When she spoke, her voice carried uncertainty—a function encountering variables it couldn't calculate."
  - line: 1757
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I don't know. The Spires feel... different than I remember. Changed. The Queen's corruption ran deeper than just this pyramid. There are patterns in the network I don't recognize. Equations that don't resolve.\""
  - line: 1758
    type: narration
    text: "She looked at Geralt. \"Something is wrong. But I can't see what.\""
  - line: 1760
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Could it be a trap?\""
  - line: 1762
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Perhaps.\""
  - line: 1763
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire stepped back from the Spire. \"Or perhaps I simply need time to understand. I've been imprisoned for so long, my perception is... incomplete.\" She gestured at the cistern. \"This sanctuary was built to protect the Light. Now it's cleansed. But the greater network?\" She shook her head. \"I need to study. To observe. To understand what changed while I was trapped.\""
  - line: 1765
    type: narration
    text: "Relief flooded through Geralt."
  - line: 1766
    type: narration
    text: "She wasn't rushing to activate anything."
  - line: 1767
    type: narration
    text: "Wasn't assuming victory."
  - line: 1769
    type: narration
    text: "She was being careful."
  - line: 1771
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"How long?\""
  - line: 1773
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"To fully understand the network's current state?\""
  - line: 1774
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire considered. \"Months. Perhaps years. The Spires are complex—Graviton technology woven with planetary harmonics. Each one is unique. I need to examine them individually, trace the changes, identify any remaining corruption.\""
  - line: 1776
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And until then?\""
  - line: 1777
    type: narration
    text: "Mika pressed."
  - line: 1779
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I rest. I recover. I remain free.\""
  - line: 1780
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's smile was small but genuine. \"I am whole for the first time in centuries. I can wait a while longer before attempting anything that might endanger that.\""
  - line: 1782
    type: narration
    text: "She looked at the assembled Legion—exhausted, wounded, victorious."
  - line: 1784
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You saved me. I will not waste that gift by acting rashly.\""
  - line: 1785
    type: narration
    text: "Her gaze returned to Geralt and Mika. \"You taught me that caring means choosing carefully. That rushing ahead without understanding costs lives.\" She gestured at the bond between them. \"You showed me that partnership requires patience.\""
  - line: 1787
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"So the Spires stay dormant,\""
  - line: 1788
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt confirmed."
  - line: 1790
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"For now. Until I understand what I'm truly facing.\""
  - line: 1791
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's expression turned serious. \"The Queen had centuries to corrupt this network. I need to be certain that activating it won't serve her purposes instead of ours.\""
  - line: 1793
    type: narration
    text: "Smart."
  - line: 1794
    type: narration
    text: "Cautious."
  - line: 1795
    type: narration
    text: "Exactly what they needed."
  - line: 1797
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1799
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Luminaire
    text: "\"Come on,\""
  - line: 1801
    type: narration
    text: "She gestured, and the flooded passages began to drain—water flowing away through hidden channels, revealing stairs that led upward."
  - line: 1803
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"I may not be able to activate the Spires yet,\""
  - line: 1805
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Always,\""
  - line: 1807
    type: narration
    text: "Mika took his hand as they climbed."
  - line: 1808
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the Legion followed—five hundred souls who had fought the impossible and won."
  - line: 1810
    type: narration
    text: "The Void Spire hummed quietly in the empty cistern."
  - line: 1811
    type: narration
    text: "Dormant."
  - line: 1812
    type: narration
    text: "Waiting."
  - line: 1814
    type: narration
    text: "Not activated."
  - line: 1816
    type: narration
    text: "Not yet."
  - line: 1818
    type: narration
    text: "And three thousand years in the future, that patience would matter more than anyone could know."
  - line: 1820
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1822
    type: narration
    text: "They emerged from the pyramid to find dawn breaking."
  - line: 1824
    type: narration
    text: "The swamp had transformed."
  - line: 1825
    type: narration
    text: "Where corruption had spread, now green shoots pushed through clean soil."
  - line: 1826
    type: narration
    text: "The water ran clear."
  - line: 1827
    type: narration
    text: "The jungle breathed without geometry."
  - line: 1829
    type: narration
    text: "The purge had worked."
  - line: 1831
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood on the pyramid steps, Mika beside him, and felt the new bonds humming in his chest."
  - line: 1832
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire's presence—whole now, free, walking beside them as a physical being."
  - line: 1833
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron's fire—integrated into his very biology, no longer just armor but part of his flesh."
  - line: 1834
    type: narration
    text: "And his own will, stronger for having fought for both of them."
  - line: 1836
    type: narration
    text: "Tripartite."
  - line: 1837
    type: narration
    text: "Complete."
  - line: 1839
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire materialized beside them, her form shimmering slightly in the morning light."
  - line: 1840
    type: narration
    text: "She was still learning how to hold a consistent physical state."
  - line: 1842
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"What will you do?\""
  - line: 1844
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Luminaire
    text: "\"Walk with you,\""
  - line: 1846
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck approached, armorless but unbowed."
  - line: 1847
    type: narration
    text: "His salvaged Anunnaki tech lay in pieces behind them, destroyed by his sacrifice at the shield barrier."
  - line: 1849
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Orders, Commander?\""
  - line: 1851
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt looked at Mika."
  - line: 1852
    type: narration
    text: "She squeezed his hand."
  - line: 1854
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We rest,\""
  - line: 1855
    type: narration
    text: "Mika announced. \"Three days. Real rest. Then...\" She met Geralt's eyes. \"Then we finish what we started. The final slave encampment. The Anunnaki know we're coming now. They'll be ready.\""
  - line: 1857
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Let them be ready,\""
  - line: 1858
    type: narration
    text: "Halvar growled. \"We just freed a cosmic function and purged a corrupted pyramid. What's one more impossible fight?\""
  - line: 1860
    type: narration
    text: "Laughter rippled through the Legion—exhausted, half-mad, but real."
  - line: 1862
    type: narration
    text: "They had won."
  - line: 1864
    type: narration
    text: "Not without cost."
  - line: 1865
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's armor destroyed."
  - line: 1866
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt transformed forever."
  - line: 1867
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron integrated beyond any possibility of separation."
  - line: 1869
    type: narration
    text: "But they had won."
  - line: 1871
    type: narration
    text: "And Luminaire walked free beside them, learning what it meant to care, refusing to rush toward activation until she understood what she was truly facing."
  - line: 1873
    type: narration
    text: "Today, they walked down the pyramid steps together—Commander and Commander, cosmic function learning to be person, dragon integrated into human flesh, leading a Legion that refused to accept impossible as an ending."
  - line: 1875
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the Void Spire stood silent."
  - line: 1876
    type: narration
    text: "Dormant."
  - line: 1877
    type: narration
    text: "Uncorrupted."
  - line: 1879
    type: narration
    text: "But not activated."
  - line: 1881
    type: narration
    text: "Ahead, the jungle grew green."
  - line: 1883
    type: narration
    text: "And somewhere in the distance, the final slave encampment waited, fully alert, fully prepared, knowing that Ragnarok was coming."
  - line: 1885
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1887
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"*END CHAPTER 39*\""
  - line: 1889
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"

